# TimeTracker — Project Rules & Memory

## What this app is
A native macOS menu bar time tracker. No Dock icon. No screenshots. No activity monitoring.
Timer with start/stop, manual time entry (duration or time range), visual 24-hour timeline, statistics, export/import, and system notifications.

## Stack
- Swift + SwiftUI, minimum macOS 13
- Swift Package Manager (no Xcode project)
- Run with: `swift run` | Build: `swift build -c release`
- Frameworks: AppKit, SwiftUI, Combine, Foundation, UserNotifications

## Architecture

### Entry point
`main.swift` — creates `NSApplication`, sets `.accessory` activation policy (hides Dock icon), attaches `AppDelegate`, calls `app.run()`.
Do NOT use `@main` App struct — it conflicts with `main.swift`.

### AppDelegate
Owns the `NSStatusItem` and the `NSPanel` popup.
- Status bar button image is a custom-drawn `NSImage` (non-template) with pill border, colored icon and time text.
- Popup is a `KeyablePanel: NSPanel` subclass (overrides `canBecomeKey` / `canBecomeMain` to `true`) with `.borderless` + `.nonactivatingPanel`. Background is `NSVisualEffectView` (`.popover` material, corner radius 12). The `canBecomeKey` override is required so SwiftUI `TextField` can receive focus in a borderless panel.
- Panel positioned flush below menu bar button via `button.window?.convertToScreen(...)` + `setFrameTopLeftPoint`.
- Panel dismissal: global `NSEvent` monitor (outside clicks) + `NSApplication.didResignActiveNotification` (Cmd+Tab / app switch). Both check `suppressAutoClose` flag before closing.
- `suppressAutoClose: Bool` — set to `true` before running any NSSavePanel / NSOpenPanel / NSAlert modal to prevent the panel from closing underneath them.
- `withPanelLowered(_:)` — temporarily sets panel level to `.normal` before a modal runs (so the modal appears above the panel), then restores it.
- Sleep/screensaver: observes `NSWorkspace.willSleepNotification` and `com.apple.screensaver.didstart` (DistributedNotificationCenter). Calls `TimerManager.stop(reason:)`.
- Notifications: sets itself as `UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate`, requests `.alert + .sound` on launch (guarded by `Bundle.main.bundleIdentifier != nil`). Delegate returns `.banner + .sound` so notifications appear while app is active.

### TimerManager (singleton)
`TimerManager.shared` — `ObservableObject`.
- `start()` / `stop(reason:)` / `reset()`.
- `addTime(hours:minutes:note:)` — places session in latest free slot today (throws `ManualEntryError`).
- `addTimeRange(start:end:note:)` — records explicit range, validates today/future/overlap (throws `ManualEntryError`).
- `loadTodayTime()` — called once at launch to seed `elapsedSeconds`.
- `notify(title:body:)` — sends `UNUserNotificationRequest` (guarded by bundle identifier check).
- Sends notifications on `start()` and `stop(reason:)`.
- `pendingNote: String` — accumulates the note for the currently running segment; attached to the session on `stop()` and then cleared.

### SessionStore (singleton)
`SessionStore.shared` — `ObservableObject`.
- Persists to `~/Library/Application Support/TimeTracker/sessions.json` (ISO-8601 dates).
- Key queries: `sessions(on:)`, `sessions(weekOffset:)`, `sessions(monthOffset:)`, `totalSeconds(in:)`.
- Overlap helpers: `hasOverlap(start:end:)`, `findFreeSlot(duration:before:)`.
- Backup: `exportData() -> Data?`, `importSessions(from:)` (merge by id), `replaceAll(with:)`.
- `update(_:startDate:duration:note:)` — `note` defaults to `nil`; pass an empty-trimmed string as `nil` at call sites.

### ContentView tabs
Timer tab | Stats tab — `Picker` with `.segmented` style.
Timer tab manual entry has two modes (segmented picker):
- **Duration** — hours + minutes text fields; session placed in latest free slot.
- **Range** — `TimePickerField` for From/To; `DayTimelineView` shows conflict/free status.
Both entry modes include a `NoteButton` below the inputs; the note is cleared after a successful commit.
When the timer is running a `NoteButton` bound to `manager.pendingNote` appears below the Start/Stop button.

### NoteButton
`NoteButton(note: Binding<String>)` — reusable compact row that previews the note text (or "Add note…" placeholder) and opens a SwiftUI `.popover` containing a multiline `TextEditor` (`NoteEditorPopover`, 280 pt wide). Used in the timer section, both manual-entry modes, and the session edit row.

### DayTimelineView
24-hour horizontal `Canvas` timeline. Shows existing sessions (gray), selected range (blue/red), "now" marker, hour labels every 3 hours.

### TimePickerField
`NSViewRepresentable` wrapping `TimePickerNSView`. Does NOT use AppKit first-responder chain — uses `NSEvent.addLocalMonitorForEvents` for keyboard and mouse instead. Has `isActive` flag for visual focus state. Stepper ▲▼ buttons adjust the selected segment.

### SessionsListView
Session rows display the note (if non-empty) below the duration in small italic secondary text. The inline edit row includes a `NoteButton` for add/edit/clear; the note is loaded from the session on `beginEdit` and saved via `store.update(_:startDate:duration:note:)`.

### TimeSession
`note: String?` — optional free-text annotation. Field is optional in the JSON so existing sessions without it decode correctly (set to `nil`).

### StatsView
- Week view: bar chart Mon–Sun, today highlighted.
- Month view: bar chart per calendar week.
- Footer: period total + daily average (days with data only).
- Export: `NSSavePanel` → JSON file of all sessions.
- Import: `NSOpenPanel` → decode with `.iso8601` date strategy → `NSAlert` showing new/duplicate counts with Merge / Replace / Cancel options.

### Menu bar icon colors
- **Idle** (no time): `labelColor`
- **Running**: `systemGreen`
- **Paused with time**: `systemOrange`

## Key patterns & gotchas
- SF Symbol coloring in off-screen `NSImage`: use `NSImage.SymbolConfiguration(paletteColors:)` — NOT `contentTintColor`, NOT `attributedTitle`, NOT `destinationIn`.
- `MenuBarExtra` label colors are stripped — always use `NSStatusItem` with custom `NSImage`.
- `onChange(of:)` — single-arg form `{ newValue in }` for macOS 13. Two-arg `{ _, new in }` requires macOS 14+.
- Borderless `NSPanel` returns `canBecomeKey = false` — subclass and override to allow SwiftUI text field focus.
- `UNUserNotificationCenter.current()` crashes without a bundle identifier — always guard with `Bundle.main.bundleIdentifier != nil` before calling.
- Modal dialogs (NSSavePanel, NSOpenPanel, NSAlert) appear behind a `.popUpMenu` level panel — use `withPanelLowered(_:)` and `suppressAutoClose` around every modal call.
- Import JSON must use `JSONDecoder` with `.iso8601` date strategy to match the encoder.

## Git workflow
- Every new feature or bug fix MUST be developed on a dedicated branch created from `main`.
- Branch naming: `feature/<short-description>` or `fix/<short-description>`.
- Once work is complete, push the branch and open a pull/merge request against `main`.
- Direct commits to `main` are not allowed.

## Commit message conventions (Conventional Commits)
All commit messages MUST follow this format:
```
<type>[optional scope]: <short description>

[optional body]
```

Types and their effect on the release version:
- `fix:` — bug fix → **patch** bump (e.g. v1.0.0 → v1.0.1)
- `feat:` — new feature → **minor** bump (e.g. v1.0.0 → v1.1.0)
- `feat!:` or any type with `!` or body containing `BREAKING CHANGE:` → **major** bump (e.g. v1.0.0 → v2.0.0)
- `chore:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `style:` — no version bump on their own (patch unless combined with feat/breaking)

Examples:
```
fix: reset timer to 00:00:00 on new day
feat: add Pomodoro mode
feat!: replace session format with new schema
chore: update dependencies
docs: update README contributing section
```

The CI release workflow reads all commits since the last tag and picks the highest applicable bump type automatically.
